Hi Martin,

That's exactly what you would expect to see, which is why you do a QQ 
plot in the first place. On one axis you plot the expected (uniform) 
distribution of p-values, and on the other axis you plot the observed 
p-values. The p-values that deviate from the expectation are then 
possible true positives.

Best,

Jim


